## 2. Distribute Coins in Binary Tree (LeetCode 979)

**Concepts:** DFS, Postorder Traversal, Recursion

### Approach
- Each node should contain exactly one coin.
- Calculate the excess coins or shortage from each subtree.
- Transfer the excess to the parent node.
- Count the total movements required.

### Java Solution

```java
class Solution {
    int moves = 0;

    public int distributeCoins(TreeNode root) {
        moves = 0;
        dfs(root);
        return moves;
    }

    private int dfs(TreeNode node) {
        if (node == null) return 0;

        int left = dfs(node.left);
        int right = dfs(node.right);

        moves += Math.abs(left) + Math.abs(right);

        return node.val + left + right - 1;
    }
}
```

**Time Complexity:** O(n)  
**Space Complexity:** O(h)

