## 4. Delete Leaves With a Given Value (LeetCode 1325)

**Concepts:** Postorder Traversal, DFS, Recursion

### Approach
- Recursively process the left and right subtrees.
- After processing children, check whether the node is a leaf.
- If the leaf value matches the target, remove it.
- This also handles newly created leaves after deletion.

### Java Solution

```java
class Solution {
    public TreeNode removeLeafNodes(TreeNode root, int target) {
        if (root == null) return null;

        root.left = removeLeafNodes(root.left, target);
        root.right = removeLeafNodes(root.right, target);

        if (root.left == null && root.right == null
            && root.val == target) {
            return null;
        }

        return root;
    }
}
```

**Time Complexity:** O(n)  
**Space Complexity:** O(h)

