## 5. Maximum Sum BST in Binary Tree (LeetCode 1373)

**Concepts:** Postorder DFS, BST Validation, Tree Recursion

### Approach
- Recursively calculate information about each subtree.
- Check whether the current subtree is a valid BST.
- Track the minimum, maximum and sum of the subtree.
- Update the maximum BST sum whenever a valid BST is found.

### Java Solution

```java
class Solution {
    int maxSum = 0;

    class Info {
        boolean isBST;
        int min, max, sum;

        Info(boolean isBST, int min, int max, int sum) {
            this.isBST = isBST;
            this.min = min;
            this.max = max;
            this.sum = sum;
        }
    }

    public int maxSumBST(TreeNode root) {
        maxSum = 0;
        dfs(root);
        return maxSum;
    }

    private Info dfs(TreeNode node) {
        if (node == null) {
            return new Info(true, Integer.MAX_VALUE,
                            Integer.MIN_VALUE, 0);
        }

        Info left = dfs(node.left);
        Info right = dfs(node.right);

        if (left.isBST && right.isBST
            && node.val > left.max
            && node.val < right.min) {

            int sum = node.val + left.sum + right.sum;
            maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, sum);

            return new Info(
                true,
                Math.min(node.val, left.min),
                Math.max(node.val, right.max),
                sum
            );
        }

        return new Info(false, 0, 0, 0);
    }
}
```

**Time Complexity:** O(n)  
**Space Complexity:** O(h)

